A certain sum of money amounts to $15,300$ dollars after $3$ years at an annual interest rate of $6\%$, compounded semi-annually. What is the principal sum of money?
Answer
Let the principal be $P$ and the number of interest compounding per year be $n$.

When compounding semi-annually, we set $n=2$.

Using the given formula, we got $$P=\frac{15300}{(1+\frac{0.06}{2})^{3x2}} = 12500$$
